<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZCC refuses Tip Top clearance on New American.</title>
<headline>NZCC refuses Tip Top clearance on New American.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The anti-monopolies New Zealand Commerce Commission said on Tuesday it had declined clearance for Tip Top Ice Cream Ltd to buy the names and business of New American Ice Cream.</p>
<p>Although there were no dominance concerns in the frozen novelities/scoop ice cream and frozen desserts market, the commission was unsatisfied Tip Top would not acquire a dominant position. -- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
